# A STATIC COMMITTED FIXTURE (EP-28X W3). It is NEVER the live board of record.
#
# It exists so that ONE row can drive a FOLD-TIME refusal all the way out of `main()`.
# Every other DISAMBIGUATED red world in `tests/test_board_tool.py` is exercised against a
# line list built by value, which reaches `fold()` directly. This file reaches it through
# the file path, so the refusal is proved to arrive at a CALLER as a named refusal with a
# line number and the declared code — never as a traceback. The refusal is raised in
# `fold()` rather than in the read, which is a path the read-time refusals do not cover.
#
# The DISAMBIGUATED below names `2026-03-02 CLOSED`. ITEM-A has no `CLOSED` event at all,
# so the reference resolves to ZERO earlier events. That is not informational residue the
# way an unpinned `CORRECTED` reference is: this verb's reference IS its whole content, so
# the fold refuses the file WHOLE rather than letting a state claim that could not act
# read as one that landed.
#
# The extension is deliberately NOT `.log`: the repository's .gitignore matches `*.log`,
# so a fixture named that way would be untracked and absent from a fresh clone while the
# suite that needs it stayed green here.
# ==================== SEED BLOCK ====================
EVT | 2026-02-01 | ITEM-A | AUTHORED | seat | the seed
# ================== END SEED BLOCK ==================
EVT | 2026-03-01 | ITEM-A | HELD(on: a world) | seat |
EVT | 2026-03-01 | ITEM-A | OWED(by: seat, act: a ruling) | seat |
EVT | 2026-03-02 | ITEM-A | ACCEPTED | seat | ambiguous: it names neither open state
EVT | 2026-03-04 | ITEM-A | DISAMBIGUATED(ending: 2026-03-02 CLOSED, ended: HELD) | seat | names an ending this item does not have
